{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200 + multiprofile is the clear best performer (config_005/006: ~0.65 acc), while image-only is very weak (resnet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227). We have no data on whether combining modalities helps or hurts. 2) This experiment tests whether adding resnet50 image features via simple concat fusion to the best RNA configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) yields any benefit over the RNA-only baseline (config_005, 0.650). It keeps aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat) minimal to isolate the effect of image addition. 3) Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information next step: a positive result justifies investing in the 20+ remaining multimodal configs, while a negative or neutral result saves budget by confirming RNA-only is the right focus. It directly compares to config_005, changing only the addition of the image branch and concat fusion, making the causal interpretation clean."
}

